---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import VideoEmbed from '../../components/VideoEmbed.astro';
---

<Base
  title="The Persuasion Equation"
  description="An agent-based model of political polarization, simulating how personality and message factors interact to shape ideological change. Kilachand Honors College Keystone project."
>
  <article class="section">
    <header class="page-head">
      <p class="label">2025 · Kilachand Honors College · Keystone project</p>
      <div>
        <h1 class="page-title">The Persuasion Equation</h1>
        <p class="lede head-lede">
          An agent-based model simulating the interplay of personality and
          message factors in political polarization — how individual-level
          cognitive biases add up to population-level division.
        </p>
      </div>
    </header>

    <VideoEmbed
      id="wljUWSHTgTM"
      title="The Persuasion Equation: Simulating the Interplay of Personality and Message Factors in Political Polarization"
      caption="Presented at the 12th Annual Kilachand Keystone Symposium, April 2025."
    />

    <div class="body">
      <h2 class="section-heading">About the project</h2>
      <div class="prose">
        <p>
          I built an agent-based model to simulate information dissemination and
          ideological evolution across a population, grounded in the
          cognitive–motivational framework of Jost et al. Agents differ in
          personality traits and in how they respond to messages; messages
          differ in framing and source. The question the model is set up to ask
          is how those individual differences aggregate — whether
          population-level polarization emerges from cognitive biases operating
          at the level of single interactions, without anyone designing it.
        </p>
        <p>
          The project was completed as my Keystone project for the Kilachand
          Honors College, and presented at the annual Keystone Symposium
          alongside the rest of the class of 2025.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </article>

  <style>
    .head-lede {
      margin-top: 1rem;
    }

    .body {
      margin-top: 3.2rem;
    }
  </style>
</Base>
